# Auto push after changes

After finishing a set of code changes in this project, always:

1. Commit with a concise message (use local `git -c user.name` / `user.email` if identity is unset — never change global git config).
2. Push to `origin` on the current branch (`main` unless told otherwise).
3. Confirm the push briefly to the user.

Do not wait for the user to ask "push" each time. Skip only if there is nothing to commit, or if the user explicitly says not to push.
